sunxi_a133: no voltage calls without a gpu-supply; skip unreachable operating points

Without a gpu-supply (as on the Brick) regulator_get_optional() returns an error pointer, which
the debugfs "voltage:" and "man:0" commands tested as true and passed to
regulator_set_voltage(). The handle is now NULL when there is no supply, so those checks hold;
the sysfs scene_ctrl performance-mode voltage calls check it too.

sunxi_decide_pll() matched each operating point to the first PLL divider whose lowest rate
(13/16 of its output) it reaches, without checking it is not above that divider's output. The
399 MHz point (PLL 700 MHz: above 350, below 568) got gpu_dfs = 1 << (16 - 18), a negative
shift, and a point below 13/16 of PLL/4 read core_clk[4], past the end of the array. Such
points are now left out of the driver's clock table with an error message (the kernel's OPP
list still has them; a request for one is refused by sunxi_set_freq_safe()). Found on the
TrimUI Brick, 2026-10-18.

--- a/services/system/rogue/sunxi_a133/sunxi_platform.c
+++ b/services/system/rogue/sunxi_a133/sunxi_platform.c
@@ -362,13 +362,25 @@
